#: includes/class-doctor.php:115
msgid "Your system cron is not running"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:116
msgid "DISABLE_WP_CRON is set, which hands scheduling to a server cron job - but tasks are hours overdue, so that job is missing, disabled, or failing."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: wp-cron.php URL
#: includes/class-doctor.php:119
msgid "Add a server cron entry such as: */5 * * * * curl -s %s >/dev/null 2>&1 - or ask your host to confirm the existing one still runs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:130
msgid "Your site cannot reach its own cron endpoint"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the loopback error
#: includes/class-doctor.php:133
msgid "WP-Cron fires by the site requesting its own wp-cron.php, and that request is failing: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:134
msgid "unknown error"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:136
msgid "Common causes: password protection / basic auth on the site, a firewall or security plugin blocking loopback requests, a maintenance page, or DNS that does not resolve from the server itself. Fix the loopback, or set DISABLE_WP_CRON and use a server cron."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:144
msgid "A previous cron run appears to have crashed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:145
msgid "The doing_cron lock is older than ten minutes, which means a run started and never finished - usually a fatal error or timeout inside one scheduled task."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:146
msgid "The lock expires on its own, but if this recurs, check the Logs tab for the task that starts and never completes, and your PHP error log for the fatal."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:154
msgid "Cron can run, but the queue is behind"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:155
msgid "The site can reach its own wp-cron.php, yet tasks are overdue. On low-traffic sites WP-Cron only fires when someone visits; a long-running task can also starve everything scheduled after it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:156
msgid "Overdue tasks run on the next visit to the site, or run one now with its Run button. For a permanent fix on a quiet site, set DISABLE_WP_CRON and add a server cron every 5 minutes; use the Logs tab to spot slow tasks."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:163
msgid "Cron is healthy"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:165
msgid "A system cron is in charge (DISABLE_WP_CRON is set) and nothing is meaningfully overdue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-doctor.php:166
msgid "The loopback test passed and nothing is meaningfully overdue."
msgstr ""

